{"file":"Couchbase-0.1.0-v2.zip","bytes":180826,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"couchbase","description":"Official Couchbase plugin (MCP Server + Skills). Connect to a live Couchbase cluster, explore data, write and run SQL++ queries, optimize queries and GSI indexes, and design data models — grounded in your real cluster via the Couchbase MCP server.","version":"0.1.0","license":"Apache-2.0","repository":"https://github.com/Couchbase-Ecosystem/agent-skills","homepage":"https://docs.couchbase.com/","keywords":["couchbase","capella","database","nosql","mcp","sql++"]},{"path":".codex-plugin/plugin.json","name":"couchbase","description":"Official Couchbase plugin (MCP Server + Skills) for Codex. Connect to a live Couchbase cluster, explore data, run SQL++, optimize queries/indexes, and design data models via the Couchbase MCP server.","version":"0.1.0","license":"Apache-2.0","repository":"https://github.com/Couchbase-Ecosystem/agent-skills","homepage":"https://docs.couchbase.com/","keywords":["couchbase","capella","database","nosql","mcp","sql++"]},{"path":".cursor-plugin/plugin.json","name":"couchbase","description":"Official Couchbase plugin (MCP Server + Skills) for Cursor. Connect to a live Couchbase cluster, explore data, run SQL++, optimize queries/indexes, and design data models via the Couchbase MCP server.","version":"0.1.0","license":"Apache-2.0","repository":"https://github.com/Couchbase-Ecosystem/agent-skills","homepage":"https://docs.couchbase.com/","keywords":["couchbase","capella","database","nosql","mcp","sql++"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/couchbase-data-modeling/SKILL.md","name":"couchbase-data-modeling","description":"Design document models, choose document boundaries, and pick access patterns for Couchbase — grounded in real cluster data via the MCP server. Use whenever the user asks about document model, schema design, key design, document shape, embed vs reference, denormalization, scope vs collection vs bucket, modeling for query / index / FTS / vector search, time-series in Couchbase, TTL strategies, anti-patterns, migrating from SQL / MongoDB / DynamoDB / DocumentDB, or general 'how should I structure this data.' Also use when the user wants to create or seed a new collection or bucket (advise on document and key design first, then create and seed it with explicit approval). Does NOT do GSI/query-index tuning or \"why is my query slow\" (use couchbase-query-optimizer); does NOT write queries (use couchbase-natural-language-querying). Requires the Couchbase MCP server for verification.","headings":["Couchbase Data Modeling","When this skill applies","Pick the right reference","Step 0 — Confirm the connection (pre-flight)","The five-question design pass","Three core principles","Common shapes to recognize","Step 1 — Assess the situation","Step 2 — Apply the fundamentals","Step 3 — Spot antipatterns","Step 4 — Design document keys & placement (Couchbase-specific)","Step 5 — Recommend a pattern","Step 6 — Verify with real data (read-only MCP)","Step 7 — Writes require approval","What this skill won't help with","References"],"name_hint":"couchbase · 数据 · modeling"},{"path":"skills/couchbase-mcp-setup/SKILL.md","name":"couchbase-mcp-setup","description":"Guide a user through configuring the Couchbase MCP server in their coding agent. Use this skill when the Couchbase MCP server is installed but its connection fails or the CB_* environment variables aren't set, or when the user asks to connect to Couchbase or Capella and doesn't yet have a connection string and credentials configured. Does NOT tune your application's SDK connection or run data queries (use couchbase-natural-language-querying).","headings":["Couchbase MCP Server Setup","Step 0 — Detect the environment","Step 1 — Check existing configuration (never reveal secrets)","Step 2 — Choose where Couchbase lives","Step 3 — Get your connection details","Step 4 — Decide the access level (default: read-only)","Step 5 — Write the credentials into your client","Step 6 — Restart and verify","Setup verification checklist","Troubleshooting","References"],"name_hint":"couchbase · mcp · 设置"},{"path":"skills/couchbase-natural-language-querying/SKILL.md","name":"couchbase-natural-language-querying","description":"Turn a plain-English data question into a read-only SQL++ query, grounded in the live cluster's schema, sample data, and indexes — then run it and return the results. Use when the user wants to read or retrieve Couchbase data in natural language — \"show me…\", \"list…\", \"fetch…\", \"get…\", \"retrieve…\", \"give me…\", \"find documents where…\", \"which/what …\", \"how many…\", or an analytical opener like \"what was the average…\", \"calculate…\", \"compute…\", \"total/max/mean…\". Covers filtering, grouping, aggregation, joins, and matching stored values by range or location/distance (\"near…\", \"within N miles\"). Applies mid-conversation when a schema/setup/modeling session pivots to a data question. Does NOT handle full-text, vector, or semantic similarity search (use the Couchbase Search Service); does NOT analyze, optimize, or speed up queries or design indexes (use couchbase-query-optimizer); does NOT perform writes or run DDL (it may *suggest* a CREATE FUNCTION for the user to run). Requires the Couchbase MCP server.","headings":["Couchbase Natural-Language Querying","Step 0 — Confirm the connection (pre-flight)","Step 1 — Ground in the live cluster (before writing any SQL++)","Step 2 — Validate fields against the schema","Step 3 — Generate the SQL++","Step 4 — Run it read-only and return the results","Step 5 — Note index coverage and route the workload (don't optimize here)","Scope","References"],"name_hint":"couchbase · natural · language · querying"},{"path":"skills/couchbase-query-optimizer/SKILL.md","name":"couchbase-query-optimizer","description":"Diagnose and tune slow Couchbase SQL++ / N1QL queries. Use whenever the user asks about query performance, slow queries, EXPLAIN plans, why an index isn't being used, IntersectScan, PrimaryScan, covering indexes, partial indexes, array indexes (ANY / EVERY / UNNEST), index selection, query hints, the cost-based optimizer, the Index Advisor (ADVISE), system:completed_requests, query profiling (kernTime / servTime / execTime), pagination performance, prepared statements, or 'this query is slow / how do I make it faster.' Distinct from couchbase-data-modeling (document shape) and couchbase-natural-language-querying (query authoring) — this skill is about reading plans, designing the right indexes, and reshaping queries that already exist. Use proactively when the user shares an EXPLAIN output or a slow query. Requires the Couchbase MCP server.","headings":["Couchbase Query Optimizer","When this skill applies","Step 0 — Confirm the connection (pre-flight)","Core principles (read first)","Pick the right reference","Workflow","Anti-pattern checklist","Tooling","Scope","Version notes"],"name_hint":"couchbase · 查询 · optimizer"},{"path":"tools/review-skill/SKILL.md","name":"review-skill","description":"Review a proposed Couchbase Agent Skill for structural validity and content quality before publishing. Runs the skill validator, then applies a manual content-review checklist tuned to Couchbase access patterns. Use when a user wants to review, validate, or quality-check a skill.","headings":["Review Skill (meta-tool)","Workflow","Couchbase content checklist","TODO"],"name_hint":"评审 · 技能"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Couchbase Agent Skills","Available Skills","Prerequisites","Installation methods","Install each skill manually (Claude Desktop)","Contributing","License"]},{"path":"testing/README.md","headings":["Testing","Schema","Running","Validate suite schema + list cases — no network, no API key (default mode).","Run the behavioral evals against the model (Tier 2). Needs an API key.","Provider auto-detects from whichever key is set; force it with --provider.","Tiers","Real-harness tests (the sandbox)"]},{"path":"testing/sandbox/README.md","headings":["Manual sandbox for the Couchbase agent skills (Docker + real Claude Code)","Prerequisites","Setup","Edit .env: paste CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN (or set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY).","Defaults give you: local cluster (couchbase:enterprise-8.0.1) + local skill copy.","Usage","Automated tests","How it works","Known caveats"]}],"mcp_servers":["couchbase"],"config_names":[],"paths":[".agents/plugins/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".codex-plugin/plugin.json",".cursor-plugin/marketplace.json",".cursor-plugin/plugin.json",".github/CODEOWNERS",".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.yml",".github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md",".github/plugin/marketplace.json",".github/scripts/validate-skills.sh",".github/workflows/evals.yml",".github/workflows/validate-skills.yml",".gitignore","AGENTS.md","CONTRIBUTING.md","GEMINI.md","LICENSE","README.md","assets/logo.png","gemini-extension.json","mcp.json","skills/OWNERS.yaml","skills/couchbase-data-modeling/SKILL.md","skills/couchbase-data-modeling/references/access-patterns.md","skills/couchbase-data-modeling/references/anti-patterns.md","skills/couchbase-data-modeling/references/boundaries.md","skills/couchbase-data-modeling/references/document-shape.md","skills/couchbase-data-modeling/references/fields-and-conventions.md","skills/couchbase-data-modeling/references/keys.md","skills/couchbase-data-modeling/references/migration-from-relational.md","skills/couchbase-data-modeling/references/time-series-and-ttl.md","skills/couchbase-mcp-setup/SKILL.md","skills/couchbase-mcp-setup/references/capella-setup.md","skills/couchbase-mcp-setup/references/client-setup.md","skills/couchbase-mcp-setup/references/configuration.md","skills/couchbase-mcp-setup/references/local-setup.md","skills/couchbase-mcp-setup/references/safety.md","skills/couchbase-mcp-setup/references/tools.md","skills/couchbase-natural-language-querying/SKIL